   "id": 544229,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/5672e0d4009d9c7e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by T. Pozefsky, et al./Semantic Scholar)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the blood insulin levels in normal people (black line) and in people genetically more inclined to develop diabetes (prediabetic people, dashed line) after eating a meal.</p>\n<p>Make a claim based on this graph.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1069585,
     "content_html": "Prediabetic people start producing insulin later than normal people and produce less of it."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069586,
     "content_html": "Prediabetic people produce insulin at a slower rate, but produce more of it."
    },
